# MagicSquare Forbidden Rule

## Forbidden Patterns
- `print()` for debugging in production/test code.
- Bare exception handling (`except:` or `except Exception: pass`).
- Weakening tests to pass (`skip`, `xfail`, assertion dilution).
- Hardcoded domain constants where domain objects/constants should be used.
- Layer boundary violations against ECB dependency rules.

## Alternatives
- Use structured logging or pytest capture fixtures.
- Catch specific exceptions and re-raise when needed.
- Fix implementation rather than relaxing tests.
- Centralize domain constants in entity/domain value objects.
- Route interactions through allowed ECB direction.

## Enforcement Checklist
- No debug print remains.
- No bare except exists.
- No test weakening patterns are introduced.
- No new import-direction violations are introduced.
